# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_rust_external_crate.py" "RUST-EXTERNAL-CRATE GATE: PASS" "Rust external-crate / inline-module imports never couple to a test target" "Rust import precision: a bare external-crate import (use roff; / pub use roff;) and a 2-segment external/inline import (use roff::Roff;, or use markdown::fn where markdown is an inline mod {} in the same file) must NOT resolve to a SEPARATE Cargo compile target (tests/, examples/, benches/). MEASURED on clap-rs/clap: such names matched the ONLY same-basename file in the repo -- a TEST file (clap_mangen/tests/testsuite/roff.rs, tests/derive/markdown.rs) -- minting 3 FALSE production->test edges that SURVIVED dampening (sole, non-hub). A real in-crate module is reached via crate::/self::/super:: or a mod declaration and is NEVER a separate compile target, so the resolver now excludes test/example/bench files from the trailing-type-name fallback AND the bare-single-segment fallback (the same precedent the C# namespace _CS_TEST_SEG and Go _test.go rules already apply). RECALL-SAFE & a recall GAIN: a genuine same-basename SOURCE module is untouched, and removing a decoy lets a real in-crate module resolve UNIQUELY (measured on clap: 72 false src->test edges removed AND 12 real src->src edges gained, e.g. shells/mod.rs -> bash.rs/fish.rs/zsh.rs, with ZERO real edges lost). A genuinely ambiguous pair of NON-target modules still suppresses the fan-out (uniqueness guard intact). CONTENT-FREE: only repo file paths and Rust module-path strings cross. Deterministic synthetic crates, no DB, no network" "Rust external-crate (use roff;) and inline-module (use markdown::fn) imports never resolve to a tests/examples/benches compile target; a real in-crate module is untouched and a same-basename decoy is dropped (precision + recall gain), with the ambiguity guard intact" 9
